           # Transform garbage into "250-filler..." so that it looks like
           # one line from a multi-line reply. It does not matter what we
           # substitute here as long it has the right syntax.  The Postfix
           # SMTP client will use the final line’s numerical SMTP reply
           # code and enhanced status code.
           !/ˆ([2-5][0-9][0-9]($|[- ]))/ 250-filler for garbage

       This feature is available in Postfix 2.7.

ssmmttpp__rrsseett__ttiimmeeoouutt ((ddeeffaauulltt:: 2200ss))
