       BDAT  requests, when deadlines are enabled with smtpd_per_request_dead‐
       line. After a read operation transfers N plaintext message bytes  (pos‐
       sibly  after  TLS decryption), and after the DATA or BDAT request dead‐
       line is decremented by the elapsed time of  that  read  operation,  the
       DATA  or  BDAT request deadline is incremented by N/smtpd_min_data_rate
       seconds. However, the deadline will never  be  incremented  beyond  the
       time limit specified with smtpd_timeout.

